\title{IVC and Proof-Carrying Data}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The definitions that folding and recursion are trying to achieve, and the overhead problem that shapes every construction: the verifier has to be expressible as a circuit in the system it verifies.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Incrementally verifiable computation and proof-carrying data: the statements, and [the knowledge soundness they require](dhsorens-004J).}
        \li{Recursion overhead: what a verifier-in-circuit costs, and which components dominate (hashing, MSM, field arithmetic).}
        \li{Cycles of curves, and why hash-based systems avoid the problem differently.}
        \li{[How the security loss compounds over recursion depth](dhsorens-004N).}
    }
}
